        "title": "fix(control-ui): align skills page filter input heights",
        "body": "## Summary\r\n\r\nThe Agent select dropdown and filter text input in the Skills page filter row were vertically misaligned, and the Agent label showed the raw i18n key `common.filters.agent` instead of translated text.\r\n\r\n- Problem: The Agent `<label class=\"field\">` contained `<span>` + `<select>` (2 grid rows), while the filter `<label class=\"field\">` contained only `<input>` (1 grid row). Combined with `align-items: center` on the flex parent, the form controls sat at different vertical offsets (~25px), and `<select>`/`<input>` browser rendering differences added 1-2px variation. The i18n key `common.filters.agent` never existed in the translation map.\r\n- Solution: Add a `<span>` label to the filter input so both `.field` grids have identical row count; fix the i18n key to reference the existing `usage.filters.agent`; add explicit `height` to `.field input`/`.field select` for consistent browser rendering.\r\n- What changed: `ui/src/ui/views/skills.ts` (fix i18n key + add span label), `ui/src/styles/components.css` (add height to input/select)\r\n- What did NOT change: Skills page layout structure, filter behavior, any runtime logic, other `.field` usages\r\n\r\n## Change Type & Scope\r\n\r\n### Change Type (select all that apply)\r\n\r\n- [x] Bug fix\r\n- [ ] Feature\r\n- [ ] Refactor (requires explicit maintainer request)\r\n- [ ] Docs\r\n- [ ] Security hardening\r\n- [ ] Chore/infra\r\n\r\n### Scope (select all that apply)\r\n\r\n- [ ] Gateway / orchestration\r\n- [ ] Skills / tool execution\r\n- [ ] Auth / tokens\r\n- [ ] Memory / storage\r\n- [ ] Integrations\r\n- [ ] API / contracts\r\n- [x] UI / DX\r\n- [ ] CI/CD / infra\r\n\r\n## Linked Issue\r\n\r\n- Fixes #99990\r\n- [x] This PR fixes a bug or regression\r\n\r\n## Motivation\r\n\r\nOn the Skills page (`/skills`), the filter row renders misaligned form controls: the Agent `<select>` dropdown sits ~25px lower than the filter `<input>`, and the label text shows the raw i18n key string `common.filters.agent`. This is visually jarring and degrades the professional appearance of the Control UI.\r\n\r\nThree independent but compounding root causes:\r\n1. `.field` grid row count mismatch (2 vs 1)\r\n2. Nonexistent i18n translation key\r\n3. Browser rendering difference between `<select>` and `<input>`\r\n\r\nAll three are fixed in this single PR.\r\n\r\n## Review Contract\r\n\r\n```text\r\nRef: #99990 / PR #N/A\r\n\r\nSurface: UI / control-ui skills page\r\nBug: Skills filter row — Agent dropdown and text input vertically misaligned, i18n key raw string rendered\r\n\r\nCause:\r\n  P0: ui/src/ui/views/skills.ts:285 — filter <label class=\"field\"> has no <span> child\r\n      while agent <label> at line 265 has one; grid row count differs (1 vs 2),\r\n      and flex align-items:center doesn't compensate\r\n  P1: ui/src/ui/views/skills.ts:266 — \"common.filters.agent\" key does not exist\r\n      in ui/src/i18n/locales/en.ts common section; fallback renders raw key string\r\n  P2: ui/src/styles/components.css:963-975 — .field input/select share padding but\r\n      lack explicit height; Chromium renders <select> 1-2px taller than <input>\r\n  confidence: clear\r\n\r\nProvenance:\r\n  P0: introduced by 325d0208d04 (Goutam Adwant, 2026-06-15) — added agent <select> + <span>\r\n       to filter row, but adjacent filter <input> was not updated to match\r\n  P1: introduced by 325d0208d04 (Goutam Adwant, 2026-06-15) — same commit used\r\n       nonexistent i18n key\r\n  P2: introduced by 6ff83712547 (Peter Steinberger, 2025-12-21) — original .field CSS\r\n       without explicit height\r\n  confidence: clear\r\n\r\nBest fix: Yes — the fix addresses all three root causes at their source:\r\n  (1) grid structure made consistent, (2) i18n key corrected, (3) rendering unified.\r\n  No larger refactor needed.\r\n\r\nRefactor: No\r\nProof: source analysis + built artifact verification (grep in dist/)\r\nRisk: None — CSS-only + i18n key change, no runtime logic altered\r\n```\r\n\r\n## Real Behavior Proof\r\n\r\n**Behavior addressed**: Skills page filter row — Agent select dropdown and text search input vertical misalignment, and raw i18n key display.\r\n\r\n**Real environment tested**: CentOS 8, Node 24.1.0, branch `fix/skills-filter-align-99990`, local OpenClaw gateway instance at `http://127.0.0.1:18788`.\r\n\r\n**Exact steps or command run after this patch**:\r\n\r\n```bash\r\n# Step 1: Build the Control UI with the fix\r\n$ cd ui && pnpm build\r\n✓ built in 2.46s\r\n\r\n# Step 2: Restart gateway with new build\r\n$ pkill -f \"openclaw gateway\"\r\n$ OPENCLAW_ALLOW_OLDER_BINARY_DESTRUCTIVE_ACTIONS=1 pnpm openclaw gateway run --force &\r\n\r\n# Step 3: Verify i18n key fix in built JS bundle\r\n$ grep -o 'common\\.filters\\.agent' dist/control-ui/assets/skills-*.js\r\n# (no output — old key absent)\r\n\r\n$ grep -o 'usage\\.filters\\.agent' dist/control-ui/assets/skills-*.js\r\nusage.filters.agent        # ← correct key present\r\n\r\n$ grep -o 'common\\.search' dist/control-ui/assets/skills-*.js\r\ncommon.search              # ← new span label key present\r\n\r\n# Step 4: Verify height CSS in built CSS bundle\r\n$ grep -o 'height:38px' dist/control-ui/assets/index-*.css\r\nheight:38px\r\nheight:38px\r\nheight:38px\r\nheight:38px\r\nheight:38px                # ← height applied to all field input/select/textarea rules\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Evidence after fix**:\r\n\r\n```console\r\n$ grep -o 'common\\.filters\\.agent\\|usage\\.filters\\.agent\\|common\\.search' dist/control-ui/assets/skills-D6PbDF7D.js\r\nusage.filters.agent\r\ncommon.search\r\n\r\n$ grep -c 'height:38px' dist/control-ui/assets/index-ae3QIpa_.css\r\n5\r\n\r\n$ curl -s -o /dev/null -w \"%{http_code}\" http://127.0.0.1:18788/skills\r\n200\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Observed result after fix**:\r\n\r\n- Old nonexistent i18n key `common.filters.agent` is removed from the bundle; `usage.filters.agent` (value: \"Agent\") is used instead\r\n- Filter search input now has a `<span>` label (\"Search\") via `common.search` key\r\n- `.field input` and `.field select` now share the same explicit `height: 38px` for consistent browser rendering\r\n- Gateway serves the Skills page successfully (HTTP 200)\r\n- Both `.field` grid containers now have identical structure (2 rows: span + control), eliminating the ~25px vertical offset\r\n<img width=\"1892\" height=\"651\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b83e132d-73d6-43a1-80ee-da616bd2f794\" />\r\n\r\n\r\n**What was not tested**:\r\n\r\n- Visual browser rendering across different browsers/OS combinations (only verified via CSS + HTML structure analysis)\r\n- Mobile/tablet responsive layout at narrow viewports\r\n- Dark mode theme compatibility (no theme-specific CSS rules changed)\r\n\r\n### Verification environment (supplementary)\r\n\r\n- OS: CentOS 8 (Linux 4.19.112-2.el8.x86_64)\r\n- Runtime: Node 24.1.0\r\n- Model/provider: N/A (Control UI change)\r\n- Integration/channel: N/A\r\n- Relevant config (redacted): N/A\r\n\r\n## Risks and Mitigations\r\n\r\n- **Highest risk area**: `.field input`/`.field select` shared height rule — if any `.field` variant uses a substantially different font-size, the fixed `height: 38px` might clip text\r\n- **Mitigation**: The existing padding (8px top + 8px bottom) plus the inherited 14px/1.55 font from `body` yields ~30px of content height, well within 38px. `textarea` already has `min-height: 160px` which overrides `height` per CSS spec. All other `.field` usages in the app (cron, channels, workboard) already share the same font and padding.\r\n- **Compatibility impact**: Not a breaking change. This is a CSS visual fix and an i18n key correction with no API, config, or runtime behavior impact.\r\n\r\n## Security Impact\r\n\r\n- [x] New permissions/capabilities? No\r\n- [x] Secrets/tokens handling changed? No\r\n- [x] New/changed network calls? No\r\n- [x] Command/tool execution surface changed? No\r\n- [x] Data access scope changed? No\r\n\r\n## Compatibility / Migration\r\n\r\n- [x] Backward compatible? Yes\r\n- [x] Config/env changes? No\r\n- [x] Migration needed? No\r\n\r\n## Human Verification\r\n\r\n- **Verified scenarios**: Local gateway build + serve, i18n keys present in JS bundle, height CSS present in CSS bundle, page returns HTTP 200\r\n- **Edge cases checked**: `textarea` `min-height` still respected (160px overrides 38px), `.field` grid structure identical after fix\r\n- **What you did NOT verify**: Cross-browser visual rendering, mobile viewport behavior, dark mode\r\n\r\n## AI Assistance 🤖\r\n\r\n- **AI-assisted**: Yes\r\n- **Co-Authored-By**: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\r\n- **Human confirmed understanding of code changes**: Yes\r\n- **AI prompts / session excerpts**: Issue analysis identified three root causes (P0/P1/P2) via source inspection and git blame provenance. Fix applied the minimal code change for each.\r\n\r\n## Diagrams / Screenshots\r\n\r\n- **Before**: Agent `<select>` sits ~25px below filter `<input>`; label shows raw text `common.filters.agent`\r\n- **After**: Both controls aligned on the same baseline; Agent label reads \"Agent\"; filter has \"Search\" label\r\n\r\nFixes #99990\r\n\n",
